.TH snip-trash 1  "snip 0.6.0" "Snip Manual"
.SH "NAME"
snip\-trash \- manage the soft\-deletion lifecycle
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBsnip delete\fR [\fB\-\-if\-hash\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> 
\fBsnip trash\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
\fBsnip restore\fR [\fB\-\-folder\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> 
\fBsnip purge\fR [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fISELECTOR\fR> 
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
Manage soft\-deleted snippets. delete moves a snippet package into the library trash and records its original path. trash lists entries and their entry_id. restore moves an entry back, optionally to another folder. purge permanently removes an entry and requires \-\-yes.
.PP
restore and purge select a trash entry by entry_id, not by the snippet UUID. A restore fails with conflict when the destination is occupied. Purge is irreversible.
.PP
Global options are described in snip(1).
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "snip delete"
.PP
Move a snippet to the library trash
.TP
\fB\-\-if\-hash\fR \fI<IF_HASH>\fR
Refuse the write unless the snippet still has this fingerprint
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Bypass fingerprint checks and locked\-snippet protection
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISELECTOR\fR>
Snippet title, UUID prefix, or package path
.SS "snip trash"
.PP
List deleted snippets
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS "snip restore"
.PP
Restore a deleted snippet
.TP
\fB\-\-folder\fR \fI<FOLDER>\fR
Restore into this folder instead of the original location
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISELECTOR\fR>
Trash entry ID or unique prefix
.SS "snip purge"
.PP
Permanently remove a trash entry
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Confirm permanent deletion without an interactive prompt
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fISELECTOR\fR>
Trash entry ID or unique prefix
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
Soft\-delete a snippet after checking its fingerprint:
.RS 4
.nf
snip delete 79d92dea \-\-if\-hash 472697ff761e33cf
.fi
.RE
.PP
List trash as JSON and restore one entry elsewhere:
.RS 4
.nf
snip \-\-output json trash
snip restore 4401c19c \-\-folder Recovered
.fi
.RE
